[2025-07-30 12:45:00] BUGFIX: Undefined Variable Ternak Error

## Issue
Error: "Undefined variable $ternak" in index_report_penjualan.blade.php line 74

## Root Cause
Controller using wrong service method that returns 'livestockForView' instead of 'ternakForView'

## Fix Applied

### 1. Controller Method Update
Changed from `prepareSalesReportData()` to `preparePenjualanReportData()`:
```php
// Before
$data = $this->indexService->prepareSalesReportData();

// After
$data = $this->indexService->preparePenjualanReportData();
```

### 2. View Variable Update
Updated JavaScript to use correct variable name:
```php
// Before
var ternakData = @json($ternak);

// After
var ternakData = @json($ternakForView);
```

## Service Method Analysis
- `prepareSalesReportData()`: returns 'livestockForView' (for livestock data)
- `preparePenjualanReportData()`: returns 'ternakForView' (for ternak/penjualan data)

## Files Modified
- app/Http/Controllers/ReportsController.php (indexPenjualan method)
- resources/views/pages/reports/index_report_penjualan.blade.php (JavaScript variable)

## Testing Status
- [x] Undefined variable error fixed
- [x] Correct service method used
- [x] View receives proper data structure
- [x] JavaScript console.table works correctly

## Notes
- Different report types need different data structures
- Sales report uses livestock data
- Penjualan report uses ternak data
- Service methods should match the intended data type 